      "text": "We can see that $F_1$ and $F_2$ are the vertices of an ellipse with major axis length 2 and minor axis length $\\sqrt{5}/4$.\n\nSince $|PF_1 - PF_2| = 1,$ this is a hyperbola, according to the definition.\n\nThe standard equation of an ellipse with center $(h, k)$ and major axis length $2a$ is\n\\[\\frac{(x - h)^2}{a^2} + \\frac{(y - k)^2}{b^2} = 1.\\]Changing the equation to the form $a^2 - (y - k)^2 = x^2 \\over 4,$ we see that $a = \\sqrt{4/5}.$\n\nThe distance between the foci of the ellipse is $2c = 2\\sqrt{1^2 - \\left(1/4\\right)^2} = 2\\sqrt{5}/4 = \\sqrt{5}/2$.\n\nSince the distance between the foci is $2c,$ the distance between them on the y-axis is $c = \\sqrt{5}/4.$\n\nThus, $b^2 = a^2 - c^2 = (4/5) - (5/16) = 16/80 - 25/160 = 20/160 = 1/8.$\n\nTherefore, $h = -3, k = 1 - \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}, a = \\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{5}, b = \\frac{\\sqrt{20}}{8} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4},$ and $ab = \\frac{2\\sqrt{20}}{20} = \\boxed{1}.$",
